This repository is the PUBLIC compliance-documentation hub of the Journey of
Life marketplace (jolarca-dev). It is published for transparency: it indexes
architecture decisions, describes the system for SOC 2 purposes, and points at
upstream evidence by reference and cryptographic hash.

Publication is deliberate; a licence to redistribute is not.

PERMITTED USE. You may read this repository, cite it, and use it to understand
the compliance posture of the jolarca-dev fleet.

RESTRICTIONS. No part of this repository may be copied, mirrored, republished,
sold, or incorporated into a derivative work, dataset, or training corpus
without prior written authorization from Journey of Life, except for brief
quotations with attribution.

CONTENT ABSTRACTION CAP. Everything published here is abstraction-capped by
design (ADR DOC-0002): it describes component roles, data categories, trust
boundaries, and control status only. It contains no hostnames, network
addresses, ports, database identifiers, key material, or cardholder-data-environment
segmentation detail. Those live in private upstream repositories and are
referenced here by pointer and SHA-256 digest only. If you believe you have
found a control-plane identifier in this repository, treat it as a security
incident and report it under SECURITY.md — do not open a public issue.

UPSTREAM OWNERSHIP. This repository owns no fact that another repository owns.
Authoritative architecture, network policy, DPIAs, and the asset inventory
remain in their originating repositories; this hub indexes and verifies them,
it does not supersede them.

Trademarks, logos, and the Journey of Life name are not licensed by this notice.
